|~ `::builtin`, the descriptor of a primitive, and what is declared
   under it: its constructor and its refusal, and the refusals of the
   kernel no reader reaches by a query, the table of primitives, the
   tree the evaluator does not know, the session, the printer and the
   sources of the root.
   The decisions it exists for: [D46], [D114]. ~|

:builtin
  |~~ A builtin marks a word a host implements: the recipe of a
      function whose code the host hands, `::builtin{}`, where a word
      written in steps holds a quote.
      `::number/add | binding | get /value | get /1` answers
      `::builtin{}`, and a kind the host declares builds its values by a
      recipe that is one, `| impl ::builtin{}`.

      It is a map under its tag and runs nothing by itself: a name bound
      to one reads it as data, and a call of the word runs the
      implementation its host handed.
      ::link~(::qlang/hosts | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind[~(wraps
        |~~ A map, the descriptor, its fields flat under the tag. ~~|
    | throws :PayloadNotMapError
        |~~ `::builtin` holds its fields as a map, `::builtin{}` the step
            a host's verb or kind ends with; a payload of another kind is
            refused, and the descriptor is written `::builtin{}`.
        ~~|
    | throws :UnknownAstNodeTypeError
        |~~ The evaluator met a node of the parser's tree it has no rule
            for: a defect of the runtime, and no failure of the query,
            raised past the fail track to the host. The query is sound as
            it stands; the runtime is repaired, the node given its rule,
            and the query that met it is the case that shows it.
        ~~|
    | throws :AddressBoundTwiceError
        |~~ Two modules of the runtime bound an implementation under one
            address, a defect of the runtime found as it loads. Each
            implementation is bound under the address of the word or the
            kind it serves, one to an address, `number/add`.
        ~~|
    | throws :RefusalDeclaredTwiceError
        |~~ Two sites of the runtime declared one refusal under one
            address, a defect of the runtime found as it loads: the
            address is the tag the refusal answers by and the name of its
            page, so one site would speak for both. Each site declares its
            refusal under the address of what refused, the word or the
            input, one site to an address.
        ~~|
    | throws :RefusalFactNotDeclaredError
        |~~ A refusal of the runtime carried a fact that neither its label
            nor `::error` declares, a defect of the runtime: the facts an
            error holds are the definitions under the label that names it,
            and under `::error` for those every refusal shares. The fact
            is declared as a definition, a name, its page and the kind it
            holds, under the label of the refusal,
            `::path/IndexOutOfBoundsError/length` holding `::number`, or
            under `::error` when every refusal shares it.
        ~~|
    | throws :AddressNotStringError
        |~~ A module of the runtime bound an implementation under an
            address that is no string, a defect of the runtime found as it
            loads. The address is the text of the word's address,
            `number/add`.
        ~~|
    | throws :ImplementationNotHandedError
        |~~ A name is `::builtin{}`, or a kind ends in one, and the host
            handed no implementation for it beside its source; `:name`
            names it, and the root is refused as it is declared. The host
            hands an implementation for the name beside the source, or
            writes the name in steps, a quote, which runs without one.
        ~~|
    | throws :TableSealedError
        |~~ The table of the language's implementations is sealed when the
            bootstrap completes, and one bound after it is refused, a
            defect of the runtime: a module of the runtime binds its
            implementations as it loads, and a host hands its own beside
            its sources, never to the table.
        ~~|
    | throws :NumberNotFiniteLeakedToPrintError
        |~~ A number of qlang is a finite double. Source cannot mint an
            infinity or a NaN — the parser refuses the literal and every
            arithmetic site answers an error of its domain — so this tag
            reports a value a host installed. The print and the JSON of
            the boundary are where such a value shows: the print would be
            `Infinity`, which no literal reads back, and JSON would write
            `null`. `:actualValue` holds the magnitude as a string, the
            one form that prints. The host keeps the numbers it hands
            finite, its bindings and the answers of its implementations,
            and answers an error of its own where its arithmetic leaves
            the doubles.
        ~~|
    | throws :BootstrapSourceMissingError
        |~~ A source of the language resolved to nothing, so the root
            lacks what it declares; `:uri` names the source. The host maps
            the source in the imports of its package or in the import map
            of a browser, or hands the runtime a locator of its own.
        ~~|
    | throws :RootSourceNotDeclaredError
        |~~ A source of the root answered an error, or declared again a
            name the root holds, so its declarations stay out of the root;
            `:uri` names the source and `:tagName` the refusal, for a name
            declared again `::bind/NameDeclaredTwiceError` with `:name`
            the name. The source is repaired by the page of that refusal,
            and a name declared again takes a name of its own, the root's
            left as they are.
        ~~|
    | throws :ImplementationNamesNoBuiltinError
        |~~ A host handed an implementation beside a source of the root
            for a name the source declares neither as a `::builtin{}`
            under a label nor as a kind ending in one; `:uri` names the
            source and `:name` the name. A verb runs its steps, a
            `::builtin{}` among them a step, and a bare name reads its
            value, so a host declares its primitive as the recipe of a
            word under the label of its subject,
            `:any/fetch (::fn | returns |~~ The text. ~~| ::string | impl ::builtin{})`.
            A `::builtin{}` the host hands nothing for is refused with
            `::builtin/ImplementationNotHandedError`.
        ~~|
    | throws :SourceLoadError
        |~~ The platform resolved a `#qlang/<ns>` logical name to a path
            or URL the host could not read. The error carries `:host`
            (`:node` / `:web`), `:logicalName`, `:sourceLocation`, and
            either the underlying `:cause` or the HTTP `:status`. A host
            that ships its own catalog hands the runtime a locator of the
            sources of the language and never reaches the platform loader.
        ~~|
    | proves :isAValueOfItsOwn
        |~~ An empty descriptor is a value like any other. ~~|
        ~(::builtin{} | :c it | get [1 2] | c | type | eq ::builtin)
    | proves :endsAPrimitive
        |~~ The recipe of a word a host implements is an empty descriptor.
        ~~|
        ~(::number/add | binding | get /value | get /1 | eq ::builtin{})
    | proves :PayloadNotMapError/refusesAString
        |~~ A string payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(::builtin"hello" !| [type (get /actualType)] | eq [::builtin/PayloadNotMapError ::string])
    | proves :PayloadNotMapError/refusesAVector
        |~~ A vector payload is refused. ~~|
        ~(::builtin[1 2 3] !| [type (get /actualType)] | eq [::builtin/PayloadNotMapError ::vec]))
    ::builtin{}]

